\label{sec:radial-symmetry}

Let $U=B^0(0,1)\subset\R^n$, let $f:\R\to\R$ be Lipschitz, and suppose
\[
\begin{cases}
-\Delta u=f(u) & \text{in }U,\\
u=0 & \text{on }\partial U,
\end{cases}
\tag{2}
\qquad
u>0\quad\text{in }U.
\tag{3}
\]

